# Tracer: checked definitions reduce directly; aliases require an explicit bridge.
#
# Before (implicit candidate-graph bridge):
# trust have f fn(x, y R) R
# trust have a R
# trust a = 1
# have selected R = f(a, 0)
# selected = f(1, 0)
# Former behavior: the last line reopened `selected` as `f(a, 0)` and then
# applied structural congruence. That implicit representative search is gone.
#
# Now (verified):
have fn square(t R) R = t^2
square(2) = 4
trust have f fn(x, y R) R
trust have a R
trust a = 1
have selected R = f(a, 0)
selected = f(a, 0) = f(1, 0)
# Current behavior: a checked application on the goal side reduces once;
# alias transport is written explicitly before structural congruence.
#
# Boundary: `selected = f(1, 0)` alone remains rejected. Definition reduction
# does not enumerate equality representatives, instantiate known forall facts,
# or recursively unfold a second named definition.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/03_language_features/checked_definition_equality.lit
